IMPORT `mc15-nouns`

-- Magna Carta (1215), English translation in McKechnie 1905: CHAPTERS 49 TO 59.
-- The one-off chapters: the return of hostages and charters (49), the removal of named persons from
-- their bailiwicks (50), the banishment of foreign-born soldiers (51), the restoration of lands taken
-- without judgment and the King's respite for those taken by his father and brother (52, 53), the
-- appeal of a woman (54), unjust fines (55), the Welsh (56, 57, 58) and the King of Scots (59).
-- Terms the text does not define, taken as plain facts: hostages, charters, sureties, bailiwick,
-- relations, foreign-born, mercenary soldiers, franchises, legal and lawful judgment of peers,
-- the usual term of crusaders, plea, inquest, taking of the cross, full justice, forests afforested,
-- wardship, lord of the fee, appeal of a woman, unjustly and against the law of the land, similar
-- suit, marches (see NOTES.md, "Terms the text does not define").
-- Where the text does not say who must act or by when (49, 50, 52.2, 54, 55, 56.2, 56.3) the rule is a
-- decision function, or carries "as soon as" with no period (forks F49 to F59).
-- GENERATED from tools/templates/mc15-ch49-59.l4.in by tools/build.py; edit the template.

§ `Chapters 49 to 59 -- restorations, remissions and the Welsh and Scots`

§§ `Chapter 49 -- hostages and charters`

-- "immediately" fixes no period (fork F49).
-- src:105 | We will immediately restore all hostages and charters delivered to us by Englishmen, as sureties of the peace or of faithful service.
@ref Chapter 49 (src:105)
GIVEN `they were delivered to the King by Englishmen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are hostages or charters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were delivered as sureties of the peace or of faithful service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `ch 49 -- the hostages and charters are to be restored` IS
    IF   `they were delivered to the King by Englishmen`
     AND `they are hostages or charters`
     AND `they were delivered as sureties of the peace or of faithful service`
    THEN Obliged
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Obligation not covered`

-- src:105 | We will immediately restore all hostages and charters delivered to us by Englishmen, as sureties of the peace or of faithful service.
@ref Chapter 49 (src:105)
GIVEN `they were delivered to the King by Englishmen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are hostages or charters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were delivered as sureties of the peace or of faithful service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 49 -- we will immediately restore all hostages and charters delivered to us by Englishmen` IS
    IF `ch 49 -- the hostages and charters are to be restored` `they were delivered to the King by Englishmen` `they are hostages or charters` `they were delivered as sureties of the peace or of faithful service` EQUALS Obliged
    THEN PARTY `the King`
         MUST `restore the hostages and charters delivered to him by Englishmen as sureties of the peace or of faithful service`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 49: the King did not restore the hostages and charters delivered to him by Englishmen as sureties"
    ELSE FULFILLED

