§§ `Chapter 51 -- foreign-born soldiers`

-- "As soon as peace is restored": no period (fork F51).
-- src:109 | As soon as peace is restored, we will banish from the kingdom all foreign-born knights, cross-bowmen, serjeants, and mercenary soldiers, who have come with horses and arms to the kingdom’s hurt.
@ref Chapter 51 (src:109)
GIVEN `peace is restored` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A ForeignForce
      `he is foreign-born` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he came with horses and arms to the kingdom's hurt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `ch 51 -- the person is to be banished from the kingdom` IS
    IF   kind EQUALS `someone of another kind`
      OR (NOT `he is foreign-born`)
      OR (NOT `he came with horses and arms to the kingdom's hurt`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    THEN `Obligation not covered`
    ELSE IF `peace is restored`
         THEN Obliged
